                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p
              for some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The forgetful functor from the category of commutative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+rings"} local rings
              and local homomorphisms to the category of sets has a left multi-adjoint.
          %h2#diers_spectrum Diers spectrum
          %p
            The notion of a multiadjoint functor is used to define the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diers+spectrum"} Diers spectrum
          %h2#related_pages Related pages
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multirepresentable+functor"} multirepresentable functor
          %h2#references References
          %p The notion of multi-adjoints was developed by Diers in a series of publications.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yves+Diers"}> Yves Diers
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Catégories localisables
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Categories+localisables.pdf", :title => ""} Categories localisables.pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yves+Diers"}> Yves Diers
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Catégories localement multiprésentables
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yves+Diers"}> Yves Diers
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Une construction universelle des spectres, topologies spectrales et faisceaux structuraux
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1080/00927878408823101"} doi:10.1080/00927878408823101
          %p
            (in discussion of the notion of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+%28geometry%29"} spectra in geometry
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#Diers1980
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yves+Diers"}> Yves Diers
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Multimonads and multimonadic categories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/82552386.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Osmond2020a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Axel+Osmond"}> Axel Osmond
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Diers theory of Spectrum I: Stable functors and right multi-adjoints
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.00853"} arXiv:2012.00853
            %li#Osmond2020b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Axel+Osmond"}> Axel Osmond
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Diers theory of Spectrum II: Geometries and dualities
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.02167"} arXiv:2012.02167
          %p On other notions of adjoint functors and their relation to each other:
          %ul
            %li#ADLL24
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathanael+Arkor"}> Nathanael Arkor
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ivan+Di+Liberti"} Ivan Di Liberti
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fosco+Loregian"} Fosco Loregian
              = succeed "," do
                %em Adjoint functor theorems for lax-idempotent pseudomonads
              = succeed "," do
